<section class="access-section section-frame" id="network">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2>One account.<br />Every chain connected.</h2>
    <p>For businesses that bill and pay globally, and for developers who want any-chain payments without running a bridge.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="access-columns">
    <article>
      <span class="small-label">BUSINESSES</span>
      <h3>Bill in dollars.<br />Get paid in dollars.</h3>
      <p>Everything is priced in US dollars and settles as USDC, 1 to 1. Need a US entity too? Optional Wyoming LLC or Delaware C-Corp formation is built in, with agreements signed on NEAR.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#assets">See the products <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="small-label">DEVELOPER INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
      <h3>Read the same records.<br />Keep your own keys.</h3>
      <p>Create checkouts and invoices with an API key, get signed webhooks, and read every invoice from the opencash registry contract on NEAR. opencash never holds your keys or your funds.</p>
      <details>
        <summary>View integration overview <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="integration-details">
          <p>Inbound payments use NEAR Intents 1Click with exact-output quotes; payouts use exact-input quotes from USDC on NEAR. Account calls are NEP-366 meta-transactions signed by a passkey-derived key.</p>
          <code>POST /v1/checkouts &#123; amount, description, reference &#125;<br />POST /v1/invoices &#123; client_name, items, due_date &#125;<br />GET  /v1/invoices/:id<br />webhook: invoice.paid · payout.completed<br />contract: list_invoices · get_invoice</code>
          <p>The relayer only sponsors registry calls and USDC transfers to deposit addresses opencash quoted for that account.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
